[Music]  recently a friend of mine told me that  she felt guilty that she hadn't  accomplished more  during the last year the pandemic now  i've heard that a few times and  i have a feeling we're going to be  hearing that more and more as  vaccination rates  increase people are going to start  talking about the things they've  accomplished during the pandemic  as a way to measure their last year in  progress in things they've made and  things they've written  in money they've gained or changes  they've made to their lives that made  them better than they were in march of  2020  and it's going to seem like a  competition and that anyone who didn't  achieve very much  somehow lost but it's not a competition  and it's not a creative incubator or a  working vacation  it's a pandemic and you are not any  worse of a person for  living through a pandemic and not  accomplishing some big  project because you did the only thing  you had to  you lived you got up every day and  carried the weight of knowing that your  actions could put people in danger and  made the responsible choice to prevent  that you watched as the news got darker  and  darker and 3.3 million people around the  world  died as their government did little to  protect them  you wore a mask outside and lived with  the fear of worrying that other people  weren't wearing theirs  you watched as the understanding of this  disease became so convoluted that  people made up their own irresponsible  rules for how to handle it  you watched people protest for the  quote-unquote right  to walk around unmasked emboldened by  a fascist president who couldn't care  less if you lived or died  and then when vaccines finally started  rolling out  you watched as people denied their  efficacy  and risked extending the pandemic all  in the name of their so-called freedom  so  don't measure your last year and the  things you could have done  measure it in the things you had to do  with the unbearable trauma  of a worldwide crisis and pat yourself  on the back for waking up yet another  day because  that is the only accomplishment that  [Music]  matters  you

